OpenJev and TypeSafe
OpenJev's public helper and the TypeSafe system-one adapter informed Shingi's
letter scoring, chunk-and-anchor composition, confidence formulas, and HTTP
interface. OpenJev explicitly licenses helper/ under Apache-2.0; the TypeSafe
adapter is MIT licensed (Copyright 2026 TypeSafe AI):
https://huggingface.co/openjev/openjev/blob/5ec9e5fd2f80a6fff386779b1e5ac7e389971889/helper/shim.py
https://github.com/typesafe-ai/system-one-adapter-python/tree/adffc2eab300a4fa3c0e92252d4ffd6ceaa53700
No OpenJev weights are included. This is an independent project.

Training data
Praveenrajus / uspraveen published the JevBench transformations used here:
https://huggingface.co/datasets/Praveenrajus/jev-bench/tree/002ad22de8db2df5e0eb898b3da8072dbd4af4de
The underlying sources retain their own licenses. Training uses human targets,
not hosted Jev predictions. The release does not redistribute dataset rows.

- Banking77: PolyAI, Casanueva et al.; CC BY 4.0.
  https://huggingface.co/datasets/PolyAI/banking77
- CLINC150: Larson et al., CLINC; CC BY 3.0.
  https://huggingface.co/datasets/clinc/clinc_oos
- MMLU: Hendrycks et al.; MIT.
  https://huggingface.co/datasets/cais/mmlu
- ARC Challenge: Peter Clark et al., Allen Institute for AI; CC BY-SA 4.0.
  https://huggingface.co/datasets/allenai/ai2_arc
- HelpSteer2: Zhilin Wang et al., NVIDIA; CC BY 4.0.
  https://huggingface.co/datasets/nvidia/HelpSteer2
- Measuring Hate Speech: Kennedy et al., UC Berkeley D-Lab; CC BY 4.0.
  https://huggingface.co/datasets/ucberkeley-dlab/measuring-hate-speech
- BoolQ: Christopher Clark et al., Google; CC BY-SA 3.0.
  https://huggingface.co/datasets/google/boolq
- Civil Comments: Jigsaw / Civil Comments; CC0 1.0.
  https://huggingface.co/datasets/google/civil_comments

Shingi transforms the benchmark records into candidate-letter prompts, uses
paired randomized option orders during training, selects a LoRA checkpoint on
development NLL, and fits global calibration on a separate split. These are
Shingi changes; no upstream author endorses the resulting model.

Dataset terms are separate from the repository's software license. Additional
sources are used only for evaluation; see docs/release.md for the source review.

